WEBVTT

02:56.084 --> 02:58.917
SOLARIS

02:59.584 --> 03:03.792
Part One

07:09.042 --> 07:10.751
Kris, come here.

07:12.042 --> 07:13.376
You're just in time.

07:14.542 --> 07:17.334
He takes a walk every morning
for at least an hour.

07:17.542 --> 07:20.042
I forbade him to come back earlier.

07:20.292 --> 07:23.334
He's had a lot of work,
sometimes staying up all night.

07:23.542 --> 07:26.084
These Solarists.

07:27.084 --> 07:30.917
He reminds me of a bookkeeper,
preparing his accounts.

07:32.667 --> 07:34.292
We expected you yesterday.

07:34.959 --> 07:37.251
He wanted to run away
when he saw me.

07:41.167 --> 07:42.251
Hello.

07:47.042 --> 07:48.084
Hello.

07:53.584 --> 07:56.626
I probably shouldn't have
bothered you today.

08:00.917 --> 08:04.792
How old you and I have become.
I've only just realised that.

08:05.751 --> 08:07.084
What are you apologising for?

08:08.209 --> 08:09.500
Does he understand
that everything depends

08:09.501 --> 08:11.876
on his first report
from the station?

08:12.126 --> 08:16.042
Everything we've received so far
has been confusing or incomprehensible.

08:16.417 --> 08:19.251
If he confirms that the work
can't continue for some reason,

08:19.459 --> 08:23.042
the station can be taken
out of Solaris' orbit.

08:24.459 --> 08:25.876
He understands.

08:26.917 --> 08:29.501
You promised to talk to him.
I brought the film.

08:29.709 --> 08:32.501
That's what I came here for.
- Yes, of course.

08:34.667 --> 08:37.876
Can the boy stay with you
for a few days?

08:38.167 --> 08:40.876
I have a lot to do
and no one to leave him with.

08:41.334 --> 08:45.334
Anna will look after him.
She'll have more free time now.

08:54.667 --> 08:56.084
When does he leave?

08:57.251 --> 09:00.292
He'll be gone by tomorrow morning.

09:11.917 --> 09:13.667
It's so pleasant here.

09:15.167 --> 09:18.958
This house reminds me
of my grandfather's house.

09:18.959 --> 09:20.751
I liked it.

09:21.251 --> 09:24.251
So we decided
to build one just like it.

09:25.459 --> 09:27.334
I don't like innovation.

10:55.542 --> 10:57.126
I'd better get going.

11:00.334 --> 11:02.459
I have a lot to do.

11:05.542 --> 11:07.042
Don't you want to see this?

11:08.376 --> 11:11.167
I've already seen it many times.

11:15.001 --> 11:17.251
On the 21st day of our expedition,

11:17.667 --> 11:19.584
radio-biologist Vishyakov
and physicist Fekhner

11:21.709 --> 11:25.792
went on an exploratory flight
over the Solaris Ocean in a hydroplane.

11:26.501 --> 11:29.584
When they failed to return after
sixteen hours, we declared an emergency.

11:30.501 --> 11:33.917
The fog was thick and we were forced
to call the search off.

11:35.042 --> 11:37.334
All of the rescue craft
returned to the station

11:37.876 --> 11:42.209
except for the helicopter
operated by Burton.

11:42.917 --> 11:45.917
Burton returned an hour after dark.

11:46.626 --> 11:49.542
Once out of the helicopter,
he ran to his quarters.

11:50.584 --> 11:52.959
He was in a state of shock.

11:53.584 --> 11:55.959
This was highly unusual

11:56.042 --> 12:01.584
for a man with eleven years
of experience in space-flight.

12:01.626 --> 12:03.376
He recovered in a couple of days,

12:03.459 --> 12:06.334
but he would never leave the station

12:06.417 --> 12:10.376
and refused to approach the window
overlooking the Ocean.

12:10.626 --> 12:12.959
Later he wrote to us from the clinic.

12:13.042 --> 12:17.459
He was preparing a statement
of great importance,

12:17.542 --> 12:20.709
one that would decide
the fate of Solaristics.

12:20.792 --> 12:24.584
Excellent.
Let's hear what he has to say.

12:27.667 --> 12:31.501
At this time,
let us give the floor to Burton.

12:32.001 --> 12:33.917
Thank you.

12:41.292 --> 12:45.001
When I first descended
below 300 meters,

12:45.501 --> 12:47.959
I had trouble maintaining altitude.

12:48.042 --> 12:50.001
There was a strong wind.

12:52.834 --> 12:56.459
All of my attention went towards
operating the ship.

12:57.334 --> 13:01.084
I did not look out of the cabin.

13:02.209 --> 13:06.876
As a result, I wound up in a fog.
- Was it an ordinary fog?

13:06.959 --> 13:10.417
Of course not.

13:10.501 --> 13:14.167
It seemed to be colloidal and viscous.

13:15.167 --> 13:17.626
It coated all of the windows.

13:18.501 --> 13:24.042
Because of the fog's resistance,
I began to lose altitude.

13:25.501 --> 13:27.459
I couldn't see the sun,

13:27.542 --> 13:31.001
but the fog glowed red
in its direction.

13:32.959 --> 13:36.834
After half an hour
I came out into a large, open space.

13:37.292 --> 13:41.834
It was almost round,
a few hundred meters across.

13:44.209 --> 13:49.334
At that point,
I noticed a change in the Ocean.

13:50.001 --> 13:52.334
The waves disappeared.

13:52.501 --> 13:55.917
The surface became almost transparent,
with clouded patches.

13:56.501 --> 13:59.501
Yellow sludge gathered beneath it.

14:00.584 --> 14:06.542
It rose up in thin strips
and sparkled like glass.

14:07.084 --> 14:11.834
Then it began to seethe,
boil and harden.

14:12.042 --> 14:15.334
It looked like molasses.

14:16.417 --> 14:21.626
This sludge or slime
gathered into large lumps

14:22.251 --> 14:26.042
and slowly formed
different shapes.

14:26.834 --> 14:29.917
I was being drawn into the fog,

14:30.126 --> 14:32.626
so I had to struggle
against this for some time.

14:34.126 --> 14:39.334
When I looked down again,
I saw a sort of garden.

14:39.667 --> 14:41.167
A garden?

14:42.584 --> 14:45.209
Attention, please.

14:45.292 --> 14:50.084
I saw shrubs, hedges,
acacia trees, little paths.

14:50.167 --> 14:52.376
Everything was made
of the same substance.

14:52.459 --> 14:56.584
Did these trees and plants
have leaves?

14:57.417 --> 15:00.292
These shrubs and acacias?

15:00.376 --> 15:04.501
No, I already said they were all made
of plaster, but life-sized.

15:05.584 --> 15:08.917
Then everything began
to crack and break.

15:10.667 --> 15:14.334
Yellow sludge poured out of the fissures.

15:14.417 --> 15:17.626
Everything began to boil even harder,
and foam appeared.

15:20.084 --> 15:22.042
You can see for yourselves.

15:22.126 --> 15:24.251
I used a camera from time to time.

15:24.334 --> 15:28.709
Everything I saw before and after
should be on film.

15:28.959 --> 15:32.626
Then I propose we interrupt
these discussions

15:32.876 --> 15:37.167
and see everything with our own eyes.

15:38.584 --> 15:43.417
All right, show us your film.
This is very interesting.

17:21.626 --> 17:23.459
Is that it?

17:24.001 --> 17:25.792
That's all of your film?

17:26.334 --> 17:28.126
Yes, that's everything.

17:28.542 --> 17:32.542
But we don't understand.
You filmed clouds.

17:33.792 --> 17:36.126
Why did you film clouds?

17:36.209 --> 17:39.709
That must be the fog
I told you about.

17:43.042 --> 17:45.251
I wasn't expecting this.

17:47.751 --> 17:51.417
All of this could be the result
of Solaris' bio-magnetic current

17:51.501 --> 17:53.667
acting on Burton's consciousness.

17:53.834 --> 17:57.667
We now know the current is not only
a gigantic cerebral system,

17:57.751 --> 18:00.167
but a substance capable
of thought processes.

18:00.251 --> 18:02.876
That hypothesis is questionable.

18:04.167 --> 18:07.167
Were you feeling sick that day?

18:07.792 --> 18:10.876
The next part is meaningless.

18:15.792 --> 18:17.626
Let's pick up here.

18:17.709 --> 18:21.126
I discovered something floating
in one of the openings.

18:22.667 --> 18:25.792
It looked like Fechner's spacesuit.

18:26.042 --> 18:29.667
Its shape was that of a person.

18:30.751 --> 18:34.459
I turned around -
I didn't want to lose sight of that spot.

18:35.501 --> 18:39.459
At that moment,
the figure rose slightly,

18:40.292 --> 18:44.876
as if it were swimming
or treading the waves.

18:48.209 --> 18:52.084
This person had no space suit,
and he was moving.

18:52.167 --> 18:54.126
I don't understand. 'Person'?

18:54.834 --> 18:57.167
Yes, person.

18:59.667 --> 19:03.001
Just a minute.
Did you see his face?

19:03.084 --> 19:04.501
Yes.

19:10.334 --> 19:12.667
What person?

19:17.001 --> 19:19.251
Who was it?

19:21.001 --> 19:23.042
It was a child.

19:23.126 --> 19:26.084
What child?
Had you seen him before?

19:26.167 --> 19:30.084
No, never.
In any case, not that I remember.

19:31.292 --> 19:33.667
When I flew closer to him,

19:35.334 --> 19:38.376
I noticed something awful.

19:38.459 --> 19:40.209
What do you mean?

19:44.584 --> 19:47.459
I couldn't make it out at first.

19:47.917 --> 19:53.209
Then I saw that he was
unusually large. Gigantic.

19:53.834 --> 19:58.334
He was about four meters tall.

19:58.584 --> 20:03.126
He had blue eyes

20:03.626 --> 20:05.251
and dark hair.

20:05.334 --> 20:07.959
Perhaps you're not feeling well?

20:10.292 --> 20:14.084
We'll postpone the meeting.

20:15.376 --> 20:17.667
I'll continue.

20:24.084 --> 20:28.126
He was naked, absolutely naked,

20:28.751 --> 20:31.042
like a newborn.

20:32.709 --> 20:36.667
He was wet, or rather, slippery.

20:37.376 --> 20:39.334
His skin was shiny.

20:39.667 --> 20:44.001
He rose and fell like the waves,
but he was moving by himself.

20:44.084 --> 20:47.042
It was disgusting.

20:58.626 --> 21:02.292
I'm sorry.
I'll move ahead a little.

21:03.292 --> 21:05.834
There isn't much more.

21:06.292 --> 21:11.959
Burton's statements appear to be
the result of a hallucinatory complex

21:12.042 --> 21:14.876
brought on
by the planet's atmosphere,

21:14.959 --> 21:17.084
as well as symptoms of depression

21:17.167 --> 21:20.584
exacerbated by inflammation
of the associative zone

21:20.667 --> 21:23.251
of the cerebral cortex.

21:23.334 --> 21:26.542
This report in no way,
or in almost no way,

21:26.626 --> 21:29.001
corresponds with reality.

21:29.876 --> 21:32.334
What do you mean 'almost'?

21:32.417 --> 21:35.251
Excuse me, I'm not finished yet.

21:35.334 --> 21:39.126
Professor Messenger
offers a different opinion.

21:39.209 --> 21:44.292
He believes that Burton's statements
could be founded in reality

21:44.376 --> 21:48.667
and merit further study.

21:48.751 --> 21:50.292
That's it.

21:51.834 --> 21:54.251
I saw it all with my own eyes.

21:57.959 --> 22:01.292
I would like to offer
another opinion.

22:02.084 --> 22:05.501
We stand on the brink
of an enormous discovery,

22:05.751 --> 22:10.834
Our decision should not rely
on the observations

22:10.917 --> 22:15.667
of a man without
any scientific qualifications.

22:16.542 --> 22:20.709
Although any researcher
may envy this pilot,

22:21.167 --> 22:25.501
his presence of mind,
his gift of observation.

22:26.209 --> 22:29.751
Moreover, in light
of recent information,

22:30.292 --> 22:35.959
we are morally obligated
to continue the exploration.

22:36.834 --> 22:39.584
I can understand
how Professor Messenger feels.

22:39.667 --> 22:41.376
I understand him.

22:41.459 --> 22:44.501
But let's take a look
at the road we've travelled.

22:44.626 --> 22:50.584
Solaristics is exactly
where it began.

22:51.084 --> 22:54.584
Years of work have been in vain.

22:57.834 --> 23:02.751
Everything we now know
about Solaris is negative

23:03.334 --> 23:08.251
and has come to resemble a mountain
of disjointed, incoherent facts

23:08.334 --> 23:11.834
that strain credulity.

23:13.042 --> 23:16.417
We're in exactly
the same situation today.

23:18.167 --> 23:20.251
Solaristics is degenerating.

23:20.334 --> 23:23.042
But what we're talking about
is far more serious

23:23.126 --> 23:24.792
than just the study of Solaristics.

23:25.042 --> 23:28.709
We're talking about the boundaries
of human knowledge.

23:28.834 --> 23:32.667
Don't you think that
by establishing artificial barriers

23:32.751 --> 23:37.167
we deliver a blow
to the idea of limitless thought?

23:37.792 --> 23:43.501
By limiting our movement forward,
we facilitate moving backwards.

23:43.709 --> 23:46.167
I nevertheless repeat my question.

23:46.376 --> 23:48.251
What do you mean by saying

23:48.334 --> 23:51.251
the report of my observations in almost
no way corresponds with reality?

23:51.959 --> 23:56.834
I saw everything with my own eyes.
What do you mean by "almost"?

23:56.917 --> 24:01.792
"Almost no way" means
that some real phenomena

24:01.876 --> 24:05.167
could have triggered
your hallucinations, Burton.

24:06.917 --> 24:09.001
When it's windy,

24:09.084 --> 24:13.667
it's easy to confuse a swaying bush
with a living being,

24:14.126 --> 24:17.834
to say nothing of a foreign planet.

24:18.126 --> 24:21.667
I meant no offence, Burton.
None.

24:21.834 --> 24:26.292
I'd like to know what impact
Professor Messenger's opinion will have.

24:27.084 --> 24:29.292
Practically none,

24:29.542 --> 24:35.167
which means that exploration
in this area will be discontinued.

24:35.501 --> 24:37.334
Just a moment. Yes...

24:37.417 --> 24:39.001
I'd like to make a statement.

24:39.084 --> 24:41.459
The commission has not offended me,

24:41.542 --> 24:43.542
but it has offended
the spirit of the expedition.

24:43.626 --> 24:46.209
Therefore, I consider it
my duty to announce...

24:48.709 --> 24:51.251
And so on...

24:53.542 --> 24:56.001
Nowadays it's considered
good manners to laugh

24:56.084 --> 24:59.459
when Burton's report is mentioned.

25:01.292 --> 25:03.251
Thank you, Burton.

25:03.334 --> 25:06.959
We've known you for a long time,
but I never knew anything about you.

25:10.376 --> 25:12.751
You know, you were very handsome.

25:12.834 --> 25:16.334
That's not true,
but thanks anyway.

25:17.001 --> 25:18.792
Excuse me.

25:24.417 --> 25:27.376
Well, Kris, what do you think?

25:28.709 --> 25:30.709
If you don't mind,

25:31.792 --> 25:36.167
I'd like to speak to your son alone.

25:36.501 --> 25:40.667
I don't want to look like a fool
in front of you yet again.

25:42.959 --> 25:45.959
I'll wait for you outside by the swing.

25:51.501 --> 25:53.917
What a ridiculous man.

25:54.042 --> 25:57.292
You have no reason to say that.

25:58.209 --> 26:00.667
He's ill at ease.

26:00.917 --> 26:04.042
He thinks he's getting
in the way of our farewell.

26:07.751 --> 26:09.751
He's a tactful man.

26:09.834 --> 26:13.501
If he decided to come, it's because
he considers this important.

26:15.167 --> 26:19.626
Although, I admit,
I'd rather not see anyone now.

26:19.834 --> 26:22.167
You and I rarely get
a chance to talk.

26:28.626 --> 26:31.251
I'm glad to hear you say that.

26:32.959 --> 26:35.209
Even if it's on the last day.

26:47.501 --> 26:49.667
The last day.

26:52.751 --> 26:58.334
One always feels awful
after a big farewell.

26:59.959 --> 27:01.584
Here comes your aunt.

27:01.667 --> 27:05.001
Let's meet after lunch.
We need to talk.

27:05.292 --> 27:10.126
Why did you have to invite this Burton
today of all days?

27:12.001 --> 27:15.667
Where are the guests going to sleep?
Next to you, or in the room upstairs?

27:17.667 --> 27:20.001
Upstairs, I suppose.

27:21.501 --> 27:25.084
Well, I'm off to my meeting
by the swing.

27:25.292 --> 27:27.667
- But...
- Just a moment.

27:30.001 --> 27:32.876
You and your rooms can wait.

27:42.001 --> 27:44.167
Listen, Kris...

28:02.167 --> 28:04.042
What happened?

28:04.459 --> 28:07.417
- What's standing over there?
- What are you afraid of?

28:07.501 --> 28:09.417
In the garage, staring at me.

28:09.501 --> 28:11.084
It's a horse.

28:11.167 --> 28:13.292
Don't. I've seen it already.

28:13.376 --> 28:15.459
Come along.

28:18.084 --> 28:21.584
He's gentle.
Look how beautiful he is.

28:28.376 --> 28:34.084
You understand, I think
Solaristics has reached an impasse

28:34.167 --> 28:37.167
as a result
of irresponsible daydreaming.

28:38.292 --> 28:40.167
I'm interested in the truth,

28:40.251 --> 28:43.334
but you want to turn me
into a biased supporter.

28:45.167 --> 28:48.751
I don't have the right to make decisions
based on impulses of the heart.

28:48.834 --> 28:51.917
I'm not a poet.
I have a concrete goal:

28:52.001 --> 28:55.084
either stop the research
and remove the station from orbit,

28:55.167 --> 28:58.917
thereby legitimising
the Solaristics crisis,

28:59.292 --> 29:01.917
or take extreme measures.

29:02.001 --> 29:05.084
Perhaps bombard the Ocean
with heavy radiation.

29:05.167 --> 29:07.209
- Not that.
- Why not?

29:07.292 --> 29:11.667
Didn't you say research
should continue at any price?

29:12.084 --> 29:17.667
You want to destroy that which we are
presently incapable of understanding?

29:18.834 --> 29:22.834
Forgive me, but I am not an advocate
of knowledge at any price.

29:23.584 --> 29:28.042
Knowledge is only valid
when it's based on morality.

29:29.626 --> 29:33.751
Man is the one who renders science
moral or immoral.

29:33.834 --> 29:35.542
Remember Hiroshima.

29:35.626 --> 29:38.001
Then don't make science immoral.

29:38.501 --> 29:40.501
It's strange...

29:43.334 --> 29:46.376
Strange.
There's nothing strange about it.

29:48.334 --> 29:52.459
You yourself can't be certain
that what you saw

29:52.542 --> 29:55.209
wasn't just hallucinations.

29:55.292 --> 29:57.126
Thank you very much.

29:57.209 --> 29:59.584
It's seems there's
nothing more to discuss.

30:04.292 --> 30:06.167
- What happened?
- I'm leaving.

30:06.251 --> 30:08.001
Where are you going?

30:10.334 --> 30:12.501
He's an accountant, not a scientist.
You were right.

30:12.584 --> 30:15.751
You and I are friends, but that doesn't
mean you can say that about him.

30:15.834 --> 30:20.417
Fine. You and I have known each other for
twenty years. It had to end someday.

30:21.001 --> 30:23.417
Are you leaving the boy?

30:35.126 --> 30:38.584
What did you have to offend him for?
You're too harsh.

30:38.667 --> 30:42.959
It's dangerous to send
people like you into space.

30:43.042 --> 30:46.501
Everything there is too fragile.
Yes, fragile.

30:46.584 --> 30:50.584
The Earth has somehow
become adjusted to people like you,

30:50.751 --> 30:52.584
although at what sacrifice.

30:53.084 --> 30:57.251
What, are you jealous that he'll be
the one to bury me, and not you?

31:15.126 --> 31:20.126
Thus, it had been established that
the Solaris Ocean is a distinctive brain.

31:20.709 --> 31:24.167
Right after that, an even more daring
hypothesis came out,

31:24.251 --> 31:27.292
suggesting that the Ocean
is a thinking substance.

31:28.334 --> 31:32.001
Incidentally, this hypothesis

31:32.084 --> 31:35.709
still cannot be confirmed or refuted.

31:36.626 --> 31:39.334
It's a program about Solaris.

31:40.501 --> 31:43.542
There are few believers left.

31:43.626 --> 31:47.417
First of all, there are those connected
to the fate of the Solaris station.

31:47.626 --> 31:51.084
On this huge station
built to house 85people

31:51.167 --> 31:52.917
there is now a crew of three.

31:53.001 --> 31:55.667
They are: astro-biologist Sartorius,

31:55.751 --> 31:58.042
cyberneticist Snaut,

31:59.292 --> 32:02.251
and physiologist Gibarian,
who deal with the problem...

32:03.959 --> 32:05.876
I'm calling from the city.

32:06.084 --> 32:07.876
Burton.

32:09.501 --> 32:12.834
Anna, leave for a minute.
We need to talk.

32:19.376 --> 32:24.626
I didn't talk to Kris
about what was most important:

32:25.292 --> 32:30.167
about Messenger, who voiced
a different opinion at that meeting.

32:31.209 --> 32:35.709
He became very interested in Fechner,
who died in the Solaris Ocean.

32:37.376 --> 32:41.001
It turns out that Fechner
has an orphaned son.

32:41.084 --> 32:44.542
He had left his family.

32:45.001 --> 32:50.209
Messenger and I paid a visit
to Fechner's widow,

32:51.376 --> 32:54.334
and I saw this boy with my own eyes.

32:54.417 --> 32:56.584
You never told me about that.

32:56.667 --> 32:58.334
I never got the chance.

32:59.209 --> 33:02.501
Fine. Go on.

33:02.751 --> 33:07.751
This child was identical
to the one I saw on Solaris.

33:08.709 --> 33:11.459
Of course,
he wasn't four meters tall.

33:12.501 --> 33:15.667
He shouldn't think about this
too much before launch,

33:17.917 --> 33:20.667
but he should keep it in mind.

39:07.792 --> 39:09.834
There's no point
in keeping these papers.

39:09.917 --> 39:12.667
The ones to hold on to are in my room.

39:30.667 --> 39:35.001
My research notes, my thesis...
I held on to so much.

39:43.584 --> 39:48.126
If something should happen,
I'll find someone to take care of them.

39:48.876 --> 39:51.292
I'll come up with something.

39:51.459 --> 39:55.251
Don't look for that film.
I'm taking it with me.

39:55.334 --> 39:57.709
Remember?
The one of the bonfire?

39:57.792 --> 40:00.084
Yes, of course.

43:08.917 --> 43:12.001
- Ready, Kelvin?
Ready, Moddard.

43:12.209 --> 43:14.501
Don't worry about a thing.

43:14.584 --> 43:17.834
Have a great trip.
Send our regards.

43:18.042 --> 43:22.667
- When is launch?
- You're already flying, Kris. Take care.

43:55.251 --> 43:58.876
Solaris station. Do something.

43:58.959 --> 44:02.834
I'm losing stability.
This is Kelvin, over.

45:56.501 --> 45:58.792
Hey, where is everyone?

45:58.876 --> 46:01.251
You've got guests.

47:31.834 --> 47:33.667
Dr. Snaut?

47:59.334 --> 48:00.751
Snaut?

48:10.126 --> 48:12.667
I'm Kelvin, the psychologist.

48:14.417 --> 48:18.042
It looks like you weren't
expecting me.

48:20.417 --> 48:23.334
Did you receive the radiogram?

48:27.084 --> 48:30.751
Yes, of course.

48:46.042 --> 48:48.042
What's with you?

48:51.876 --> 48:54.792
Forgive me.

48:57.084 --> 49:00.251
Where's Gibarian?
Where's Sartorius?

49:00.667 --> 49:02.876
Sartorius is in his quarters.

49:02.959 --> 49:04.667
Gibarian is dead.

49:04.792 --> 49:06.584
What do you mean "dead"?

49:10.084 --> 49:12.626
Suicide.

49:16.001 --> 49:18.167
I beg your pardon.

49:18.584 --> 49:20.709
I knew Gibarian
and he would never have...

49:20.792 --> 49:25.542
He was almost always
in a state of deep depression

49:26.209 --> 49:30.542
ever since these disturbances began...

49:35.459 --> 49:39.542
Why don't you go rest, take a bath?

49:39.626 --> 49:44.209
Take any room
and come back in an hour.

49:44.667 --> 49:49.251
I would like to see Gibarian -
I mean, Sartorius.

49:49.584 --> 49:51.126
Later.

49:51.209 --> 49:54.667
I doubt he'd see you now.
He's upstairs, in the laboratory.

49:54.751 --> 49:56.917
Listen, Snaut,

49:57.001 --> 50:01.876
I understand that something extraordinary
has happened and perhaps...

50:08.626 --> 50:10.751
Dr. Kelvin...

50:13.459 --> 50:19.001
You understand...
Come back in an hour. Please.

50:20.667 --> 50:23.501
Go and rest.

50:24.834 --> 50:29.501
Listen, there are only three of us:
you, me and Sartorius.

50:29.584 --> 50:32.459
You know us from our photographs.

50:32.542 --> 50:35.501
If you see something
out of the ordinary,

50:35.584 --> 50:39.709
something besides me and Sartorius,
try not to lose your head.

50:39.792 --> 50:41.417
What would I see?

50:41.501 --> 50:44.751
I don't know.
That sort of depends on you.

50:44.834 --> 50:46.501
Hallucinations?

50:46.584 --> 50:50.417
No. Just remember.

50:51.001 --> 50:54.334
- Remember what?
- That we're not on Earth.

50:55.334 --> 50:59.459
You know, it would be better if you
came back in the evening, or at night.

50:59.542 --> 51:02.792
No, let's make it tomorrow morning.

52:46.084 --> 52:49.501
A. GIBARIAN

52:55.626 --> 52:57.751
HUMAN BEING

53:30.667 --> 53:32.667
FOR K. KELVIN

53:50.542 --> 53:52.667
Hi, Kris.

54:00.167 --> 54:02.792
I still have a little time left.

54:02.959 --> 54:05.667
There are some things
I must tell you,

54:06.126 --> 54:08.709
and some things
I must warn you about.

54:08.792 --> 54:12.959
By now you're at the station
and know what happened to me.

54:13.417 --> 54:17.834
If not, Snaut or Sartorius
will tell you.

54:18.834 --> 54:23.376
What happened to me...

54:26.292 --> 54:28.209
is not important.

54:28.292 --> 54:32.417
Or rather, it cannot be explained.

54:32.501 --> 54:36.459
I'm afraid that what happened to me
is only the beginning.

54:38.542 --> 54:41.251
I wouldn't, of course,
want it to happen...

54:41.334 --> 54:45.792
but this could happen to you
and the others.

54:47.084 --> 54:52.709
Here, it could probably
happen to anyone.

54:52.792 --> 54:55.417
Just don't think
that I've lost my mind.

54:55.501 --> 54:59.042
I'm of sound mind, Kris.
Believe me.

55:03.126 --> 55:05.751
After all, you know me.

55:08.042 --> 55:12.001
If I have enough time,
I'll tell you why I did everything.

55:12.376 --> 55:16.667
I'm telling you this so that,
if it does happen to you,

55:16.751 --> 55:20.667
you'll know it's not madness.

55:20.751 --> 55:22.792
That's the most important thing.

55:22.876 --> 55:27.417
As for continuing research,

55:27.501 --> 55:30.584
I'm leaning towards
Sartorius' proposal,

55:30.667 --> 55:35.834
subjecting the Ocean's plasma
to heavy radiation.

55:37.126 --> 55:41.251
I know it's prohibited,
but there's no other choice.

55:41.334 --> 55:43.001
We...

55:44.126 --> 55:47.084
You will get mired in it.

55:48.959 --> 55:54.501
It may offer a way
of breaking this deadlock.

55:55.876 --> 55:59.542
This is our only chance
to make contact with this monster.

55:59.626 --> 56:02.334
There is no other choice, Kris.

56:02.792 --> 56:05.001
If...

59:20.501 --> 59:23.876
Dr. Sartorius, I am Kelvin.

59:23.959 --> 59:26.667
I arrived two hours ago.

59:38.459 --> 59:42.501
Look, this is ridiculous.

59:46.167 --> 59:49.126
Either open up
or I'll break down the door.

59:49.292 --> 59:52.876
All right, I'll open the door,
but don't come in.

59:52.959 --> 59:55.334
- I'll come out.
- Good.

59:58.667 --> 01:00:00.959
My name is Kelvin.

01:00:03.417 --> 01:00:05.751
You must have heard of me.

01:00:05.834 --> 01:00:09.001
I work, or worked, with Gibarian.

01:00:09.084 --> 01:00:10.251
Continue.

01:00:10.334 --> 01:00:14.709
Snaut told me about Gibarian.

01:00:15.542 --> 01:00:18.751
Then you already know the story.

01:00:18.834 --> 01:00:21.751
Yes, it's horrible.

01:00:22.542 --> 01:00:25.417
I don't know the details,
but he's dead.

01:00:25.501 --> 01:00:28.792
That's not the problem.
We all die.

01:00:28.959 --> 01:00:33.584
But he insisted on being buried on Earth.
Is space really such a bad grave for him?

01:00:34.334 --> 01:00:37.417
But Gibarian wanted to be
in the ground, with the worms.

01:00:37.501 --> 01:00:40.084
I wanted to disregard it,
but Snaut insisted.

01:00:40.167 --> 01:00:43.417
- Have you ever heard of Burton?
- He was the pilot who...

01:00:43.501 --> 01:00:46.501
Yes, he was in the search party
for Fechner.

01:00:46.584 --> 01:00:49.626
Fechner died a magnificent death,
but Gibarian was a coward.

01:00:49.709 --> 01:00:53.167
There's no point
talking badly of him now.

01:00:53.959 --> 01:00:57.251
It's at least worth talking about duty.

01:00:57.334 --> 01:00:59.084
Duty to whom?

01:00:59.167 --> 01:01:01.167
- To truth.
- You mean to people.

01:01:01.251 --> 01:01:04.042
You won't find truth there. Look.

01:01:09.626 --> 01:01:13.834
Your position is absurd.
Your so-called courage is inhuman.

01:01:14.751 --> 01:01:16.501
Do you hear?

01:01:22.501 --> 01:01:26.167
Go away.
You're too impressionable.

01:01:26.251 --> 01:01:29.792
You must get used to everything.
Good day.

01:04:33.376 --> 01:04:36.376
I spoke to Sartorius.

01:04:36.542 --> 01:04:38.834
He's a terrible person.

01:04:39.001 --> 01:04:41.626
He's a very talented scientist.

01:04:48.042 --> 01:04:52.251
I think I'm a little sick.

01:04:53.167 --> 01:04:57.459
There's nothing wrong with you.
You just won't take advice.

01:04:57.542 --> 01:05:02.042
Snaut, aside from the three of us,
is there anyone else on the station?

01:05:02.126 --> 01:05:04.001
Did you see someone?

01:05:05.917 --> 01:05:09.167
What were you warning me about?

01:05:09.251 --> 01:05:11.417
Whom did you see?

01:05:11.501 --> 01:05:15.042
Was it a human being?
Is she real?

01:05:16.209 --> 01:05:20.126
Can she be touched? Wounded?

01:05:21.709 --> 01:05:24.501
You saw her today.

01:05:26.584 --> 01:05:29.709
And you?
Who are you?

01:05:35.417 --> 01:05:37.126
Quiet.

01:05:49.042 --> 01:05:52.001
- Where did she come from?
- Leave me alone.

01:05:54.667 --> 01:05:56.417
You're afraid.

01:06:00.834 --> 01:06:02.501
Don't worry.

01:06:04.459 --> 01:06:06.709
I won't think you're insane.

01:06:06.792 --> 01:06:11.501
Insane?
God, you know absolutely nothing.

01:06:11.584 --> 01:06:13.501
Insane...

01:06:14.334 --> 01:06:16.626
That would be a blessing.

01:06:23.709 --> 01:06:25.667
Listen to me, Snaut...

01:07:32.334 --> 01:07:33.876
It's all so senseless.

01:07:35.501 --> 01:07:39.709
They won't understand me.
They think I've gone mad.

01:07:49.084 --> 01:07:51.292
Do you see, Kris,
how it's not entirely absurd?

01:07:51.376 --> 01:07:54.751
I have to do this because
I'm afraid they'll come in here.

01:07:54.834 --> 01:07:56.709
I mean Snaut and Sartorius.

01:07:56.792 --> 01:07:59.417
They themselves don't understand
what they're doing.

01:07:59.501 --> 01:08:02.001
I'm afraid, Kris...

01:08:02.667 --> 01:08:04.834
I can't...

01:08:05.584 --> 01:08:08.251
Nobody will be able to understand.

01:08:08.334 --> 01:08:11.626
Open up. You hear, Gibarian?
Open up.

01:08:11.709 --> 01:08:15.834
Don't be stupid.
It's just us - Snaut and Sartorius.

01:08:15.917 --> 01:08:18.084
We want to help you.

01:08:18.334 --> 01:08:20.751
They want to help me.

01:08:21.917 --> 01:08:24.584
Just a second. Stop knocking.

01:08:34.167 --> 01:08:36.626
I am my own judge.

01:08:39.834 --> 01:08:42.042
Have you seen her?

01:08:42.709 --> 01:08:46.501
Kris, understand that
this is not madness.

01:08:49.501 --> 01:08:54.501
It has something to do
with conscience.

01:09:04.459 --> 01:09:09.001
I really wanted you
to get here in time, Kris.

01:13:54.459 --> 01:13:56.417
Where did you...?

01:14:01.126 --> 01:14:03.167
It's so nice.

01:14:16.209 --> 01:14:19.792
But... but it's not...

01:14:22.084 --> 01:14:24.667
How did you know where I...?

01:14:24.792 --> 01:14:27.167
What do you mean, "how"?

01:14:33.667 --> 01:14:36.501
Don't, Kris. That tickles.

01:14:48.126 --> 01:14:51.084
Where are my shoes?
- Shoes?

01:15:07.167 --> 01:15:10.001
No. They're not there.

01:15:21.834 --> 01:15:23.667
Who's this?

01:15:46.209 --> 01:15:47.876
it's me.

01:15:57.626 --> 01:15:59.417
You know...

01:16:02.626 --> 01:16:05.126
I have the feeling...

01:16:09.126 --> 01:16:11.376
as if I've forgotten something.

01:16:22.334 --> 01:16:24.501
I can't understand it.

01:16:29.167 --> 01:16:30.792
Do you love me?

01:16:30.876 --> 01:16:35.167
Don't be foolish, Hari.
As if you didn't know.

01:16:35.667 --> 01:16:38.501
I'm going out for a moment.
Wait for me.

01:16:38.584 --> 01:16:42.709
- I'll go with you.
- No, Hari. I'll be back soon.

01:16:46.209 --> 01:16:48.751
What is wrong? Why?

01:16:52.167 --> 01:16:55.334
I don't know. I can't.

01:16:55.417 --> 01:16:57.334
You can't what?

01:16:58.334 --> 01:17:02.792
It feels like I...
I have to see you... all the time.

01:17:04.876 --> 01:17:07.209
What are you, a child?

01:17:07.292 --> 01:17:10.167
I have work to do, Hari.

01:17:17.667 --> 01:17:20.334
I'm behaving foolishly.

01:17:22.292 --> 01:17:24.209
And so are you.

01:17:24.292 --> 01:17:28.417
Running around all dishevelled,
like Snaut.

01:17:29.626 --> 01:17:32.376
- Like who?
- Like Snaut.

01:17:34.501 --> 01:17:37.292
Listen, how do you...

01:17:40.876 --> 01:17:44.251
Well, I have to go.
If you want, we can go together.

01:17:45.876 --> 01:17:49.251
But you won't be able to get
into a suit with your dress on.

01:17:49.501 --> 01:17:51.417
Get undressed.

01:17:55.084 --> 01:17:58.001
Kris, help me. I can't undo it.

01:18:44.501 --> 01:18:46.792
Why are you looking at me like that?

01:19:06.084 --> 01:19:10.792
SOLARIS
Part Two

01:20:25.084 --> 01:20:26.917
Get in.

01:20:27.542 --> 01:20:29.334
- What about you?
- I'm right behind you.

01:20:29.417 --> 01:20:31.709
I have to shut the hatch.

01:20:34.501 --> 01:20:37.376
Is everything all right?
Are you comfortable?

01:20:37.459 --> 01:20:39.751
Yes. Hurry, Kris.

01:22:54.251 --> 01:22:56.126
You could at least knock.

01:22:56.209 --> 01:22:59.126
It sounded
like you were talking to someone.

01:22:59.459 --> 01:23:01.417
All the more reason.

01:23:01.626 --> 01:23:03.542
So you had guests?

01:23:03.626 --> 01:23:07.459
Well, I see you took
good care of them.

01:23:08.959 --> 01:23:12.376
It's nothing.
You won't die from it.

01:23:13.167 --> 01:23:15.751
Did you at least start out modestly?

01:23:15.917 --> 01:23:19.876
Narcotics, poisons, barbiturates?

01:23:20.459 --> 01:23:23.709
If you plan to behave irresponsibility,
you might as well leave.

01:23:23.792 --> 01:23:27.292
Sometimes you become a fool
without wanting to.

01:23:27.376 --> 01:23:31.584
Don't tell me you haven't tried
a rope or a hammer.

01:23:32.209 --> 01:23:36.084
Did you happen to throw
the inkwell like Luther?

01:23:44.709 --> 01:23:46.917
So,

01:23:47.626 --> 01:23:51.042
one, two, and into the rocket,

01:23:51.126 --> 01:23:52.917
and that was that.

01:23:53.667 --> 01:23:57.292
Next time, don't panic.

01:23:57.751 --> 01:24:01.959
And push the button from the corridor.
You could get burned.

01:24:02.459 --> 01:24:05.167
- What was that?
- I don't know.

01:24:05.251 --> 01:24:08.792
Then again, we've managed
to determine a few things.

01:24:10.001 --> 01:24:11.709
Who was it?

01:24:11.792 --> 01:24:15.417
She died ten years ago.

01:24:16.167 --> 01:24:20.667
What you saw was the materialisation
of your conception of her.

01:24:21.292 --> 01:24:24.292
What was her name?

01:24:32.876 --> 01:24:38.334
Everything began after we started
experimenting with radiation.

01:24:39.334 --> 01:24:43.292
We hit the Ocean's surface

01:24:43.376 --> 01:24:46.292
with strong X-ray beams.

01:24:47.792 --> 01:24:49.084
But it...

01:24:49.167 --> 01:24:53.626
Incidentally, consider yourself lucky.
After all, she's a part of your past.

01:24:53.959 --> 01:24:57.917
What if it had been something
you had never seen before,

01:24:58.001 --> 01:25:00.626
but something you had thought
or imagined?

01:25:01.334 --> 01:25:02.917
I don't understand.

01:25:03.001 --> 01:25:06.834
Evidently the Ocean responded to
our heavy radiation with something else.

01:25:06.917 --> 01:25:11.751
It probed our minds and extracted
something like islands of memory.

01:25:16.792 --> 01:25:18.501
Will she come back?

01:25:18.584 --> 01:25:20.167
She will...

01:25:20.292 --> 01:25:22.334
and she won't.

01:25:26.126 --> 01:25:29.459
- Hari the Second.
- There may be an endless number of them.

01:25:29.542 --> 01:25:31.542
Why didn't you warn me?

01:25:31.626 --> 01:25:33.709
You wouldn't have believed me.

01:25:33.792 --> 01:25:38.459
I was afraid and acted not entirely...

01:25:38.542 --> 01:25:41.959
Don't be too hard on yourself.
We've had enough of Gibarian.

01:25:42.709 --> 01:25:45.876
There's talk about
liquidating the station.

01:25:46.417 --> 01:25:49.084
That's why I was sent here.

01:25:50.459 --> 01:25:54.459
If I submit a report, will you sign it?

01:25:54.667 --> 01:25:57.834
And what if we suddenly make
that long-awaited contact?

01:25:59.001 --> 01:26:04.584
Night is the best time here.
It somehow reminds me of Earth.

01:26:05.167 --> 01:26:08.626
Attach strips of paper
to the air vents.

01:26:11.126 --> 01:26:16.626
At night it sounds like
the rustling of leaves.

01:26:17.292 --> 01:26:20.792
It was Gibarian's invention.
So simple, like all genius.

01:26:20.876 --> 01:26:22.876
I adopted it right away.

01:26:22.959 --> 01:26:27.417
Sartorius made fun of us,
but he has one in his room.

01:26:27.917 --> 01:26:30.709
He hides it in the closet.

01:26:32.084 --> 01:26:34.542
You should rest.

01:26:34.626 --> 01:26:38.292
If you can, come to the library later.

01:26:38.376 --> 01:26:41.626
I've prepared a list of books for you.

01:28:31.167 --> 01:28:33.834
Snaut, is that you?

01:28:40.834 --> 01:28:44.626
Kris, where are you?

01:28:45.917 --> 01:28:48.126
Come here.

01:30:24.334 --> 01:30:27.959
- It's so dark.
- Come here. Don't be afraid.

01:31:25.959 --> 01:31:29.084
The door opens the other way.

01:32:25.917 --> 01:32:28.792
Hold on.
I'll be right back.

01:33:17.626 --> 01:33:21.251
When I saw you weren't there,
I was frightened.

01:33:24.542 --> 01:33:26.376
Hello, Kris.

01:33:27.709 --> 01:33:30.459
I can barely hear you.
Speak louder.

01:33:31.334 --> 01:33:33.626
What are you doing right now?

01:33:34.876 --> 01:33:36.834
Nothing.

01:33:37.001 --> 01:33:41.292
Sartorius has invited us
to his laboratory.

01:33:41.751 --> 01:33:43.459
How are you?

01:33:43.542 --> 01:33:46.126
Fine. I'll try to make it.

01:34:00.209 --> 01:34:03.126
Kris, what's wrong with me?

01:34:18.667 --> 01:34:22.209
Perhaps it's epilepsy?

01:35:16.792 --> 01:35:18.834
This is my wife.

01:35:20.792 --> 01:35:22.501
Hello.

01:35:25.501 --> 01:35:27.542
Hello.

01:35:29.792 --> 01:35:32.792
- We've been waiting for you.
- I was busy.

01:35:34.459 --> 01:35:38.167
- How lovely. Are these yours?
- No, they're Snaut's.

01:35:39.792 --> 01:35:45.542
So, as far as I can tell,
they are constructed...

01:35:45.626 --> 01:35:47.709
Let's just call them 'guests'.

01:35:47.792 --> 01:35:49.584
Fine.

01:35:50.042 --> 01:35:54.834
While our structure is made of atoms,
theirs consists of neutrinos.

01:35:55.084 --> 01:35:59.376
But neutrino systems are unstable.

01:35:59.792 --> 01:36:03.292
They seem to be stabilised
by Solaris' force field.

01:36:08.501 --> 01:36:11.167
You have a superb specimen.

01:36:12.459 --> 01:36:14.709
That's my wife.

01:36:14.917 --> 01:36:17.792
Wonderful. Perfect.

01:36:21.042 --> 01:36:24.334
Then take a blood sample
from your wife.

01:36:24.417 --> 01:36:26.084
Why?

01:36:26.167 --> 01:36:28.376
It'll sober you up a little.

01:37:03.709 --> 01:37:06.542
What do you think?

01:37:08.126 --> 01:37:10.584
- Snaut?
- Enough of all of you.

01:37:12.792 --> 01:37:15.751
I burned the blood with acid,
but it's restoring itself.

01:37:15.834 --> 01:37:17.417
Regeneration?

01:37:17.501 --> 01:37:22.834
In essence, immortality -
Faust's problem.

01:37:22.917 --> 01:37:24.626
Excuse me.

01:37:28.751 --> 01:37:31.126
There's no need for cotton.

01:37:32.209 --> 01:37:35.209
Are you qualified
to perform an autopsy?

01:37:35.292 --> 01:37:38.376
I've already told you - she's my wife.
Don't you understand?

01:37:38.542 --> 01:37:42.126
I think these experiments are
more humane than testing on rabbits.

01:37:42.876 --> 01:37:44.209
Don't you agree?

01:37:44.292 --> 01:37:46.292
It doesn't matter.

01:37:46.376 --> 01:37:48.584
It would be like
cutting my own leg off.

01:37:50.084 --> 01:37:52.667
Did you feel pain
when you broke through the door?

01:37:52.751 --> 01:37:55.376
Pain? Of course.

01:37:55.667 --> 01:37:58.876
So if I ever catch you doing anything...

01:37:58.959 --> 01:38:01.626
- You're lucky.
- How?

01:38:02.501 --> 01:38:04.584
It's meaningless,

01:38:04.667 --> 01:38:07.209
yet you've managed to establish
emotional contact with them.

01:38:07.292 --> 01:38:10.501
It may be pleasant...
- What are you, jealous?

01:38:10.792 --> 01:38:12.334
Perhaps I am jealous.

01:38:12.417 --> 01:38:15.042
No, you're not jealous.
After all, you're not guilty of anything.

01:38:15.126 --> 01:38:17.167
- Of course.
- But I am guilty.

01:38:17.251 --> 01:38:18.834
Of what?

01:38:19.126 --> 01:38:23.167
When you turn into an utter cripple
with no arms or legs, call us.

01:38:23.709 --> 01:38:27.042
We'll empty your chamber-pot.

01:38:27.292 --> 01:38:30.959
- But whom have you wronged?
- You, among others.

01:39:17.251 --> 01:39:20.667
My father shot that.
Well, I shot a little.

01:42:15.917 --> 01:42:17.626
Listen...

01:42:35.292 --> 01:42:37.501
I don't know myself at all.

01:42:39.001 --> 01:42:41.084
I don't remember.

01:42:42.167 --> 01:42:46.667
When I close my eyes,
I can't recall my face. And you?

01:42:46.959 --> 01:42:48.709
What?

01:42:49.959 --> 01:42:53.626
- Do you know yourself?
- Like all humans.

01:43:03.876 --> 01:43:08.042
That woman in the white coat hated me.

01:43:08.126 --> 01:43:12.459
Don't make things up.
She died before you and I met.

01:43:14.417 --> 01:43:17.251
I don't understand
why you're deceiving me.

01:43:18.126 --> 01:43:20.334
I remember perfectly.

01:43:20.626 --> 01:43:24.709
We drank tea and she didn't want me there.

01:43:25.542 --> 01:43:28.917
Naturally, I stood up and left.
I remember perfectly.

01:43:30.292 --> 01:43:32.542
What happened after that?

01:43:34.126 --> 01:43:36.292
After that, I went away,

01:43:36.834 --> 01:43:39.792
and we never saw each other again.

01:43:40.167 --> 01:43:42.084
Where did you go?

01:43:42.334 --> 01:43:44.292
To a different city.

01:43:44.459 --> 01:43:47.126
- Why?
- I was transferred.

01:43:48.126 --> 01:43:50.626
Why did you leave without me?

01:43:52.709 --> 01:43:54.834
You didn't want to come.

01:43:57.459 --> 01:43:59.667
That I remember.

01:44:57.584 --> 01:45:01.709
Forgive me.
I thought you were already awake.

01:45:01.792 --> 01:45:03.542
What happened?

01:45:03.626 --> 01:45:05.876
The regeneration is slowing down.

01:45:05.959 --> 01:45:09.792
For two or three hours
we can be free of them.

01:45:10.042 --> 01:45:13.001
You came in the middle of the night
to tell me that?

01:45:13.792 --> 01:45:17.709
I'll tell you why I came.

01:45:18.167 --> 01:45:20.667
Sartorius and I were thinking:

01:45:21.126 --> 01:45:25.292
If the Ocean derives guests from us
while we dream,

01:45:25.792 --> 01:45:29.209
Perhaps it makes sense to transmit
our waking thoughts to it.

01:45:29.417 --> 01:45:32.626
- How?
- With beams of radiation.

01:45:33.417 --> 01:45:37.126
Perhaps it will understand
and spare us from all these apparitions.

01:45:37.251 --> 01:45:40.917
Again these ridiculous X-ray sermons
about the greatness of science?

01:45:41.126 --> 01:45:45.209
We'll modulate the beam
with the brain waves of one of us.

01:45:45.292 --> 01:45:47.667
And 'one of us' means me, of course.

01:45:48.709 --> 01:45:52.626
An encephalogram.
A transcription of all my thoughts.

01:45:52.709 --> 01:45:57.126
What if I suddenly want her to die?
To disappear.

01:45:57.292 --> 01:46:00.959
Entrust everything to that...
that mass of jelly?

01:46:01.126 --> 01:46:03.709
It's already invaded my soul.

01:46:03.792 --> 01:46:06.709
Kris, we're running out of time.

01:46:06.792 --> 01:46:11.459
Sartorius has proposed
another project: the annihilator.

01:46:11.667 --> 01:46:15.334
Self-destruction
of the neutrino systems.

01:46:17.417 --> 01:46:20.167
What is this? Blackmail?

01:46:20.459 --> 01:46:23.917
I convinced him to start
with the encephalogram.

01:46:24.334 --> 01:46:28.751
But forget about this for now.

01:46:29.959 --> 01:46:33.959
Tomorrow's my birthday.
Consider yourself invited.

01:46:34.084 --> 01:46:36.876
- Liar. You just want to make up with us.
- Yes, I do.

01:46:36.959 --> 01:46:39.584
Don't shout. She sleeping.

01:46:42.834 --> 01:46:44.626
Sleeping?

01:46:45.459 --> 01:46:48.459
She's already learned how to sleep?

01:46:49.292 --> 01:46:52.167
This will all end badly.

01:46:52.334 --> 01:46:55.251
- Well, what do you propose I do?
- Nothing.

01:46:55.459 --> 01:46:58.834
So you'll come?
Tomorrow, in the library.

01:47:02.626 --> 01:47:05.167
We'll set the table.

01:47:05.709 --> 01:47:10.417
At least there are no windows in there.

01:47:10.751 --> 01:47:12.792
In the meantime, let's go.

01:47:13.459 --> 01:47:15.459
Sartorius is waiting.

01:47:18.459 --> 01:47:20.126
She's sleeping.

01:47:20.292 --> 01:47:22.459
Will she follow me?

01:47:23.459 --> 01:47:26.084
Don't lock the door.

01:47:28.917 --> 01:47:30.667
What door?

01:47:31.792 --> 01:47:34.251
It's just an apparition.

01:48:28.792 --> 01:48:30.792
Wait. I'll be right back.

01:48:31.542 --> 01:48:33.251
Where are you going?

01:49:08.667 --> 01:49:12.126
Forgive me.

01:50:08.167 --> 01:50:10.251
Why aren't you asleep?

01:50:14.251 --> 01:50:17.542
- You don't love me.
- Stop it, Hari.

01:50:20.167 --> 01:50:23.001
- We have to talk.
- About what?

01:50:27.792 --> 01:50:31.084
You understand that I don't know
where I came from.

01:50:31.626 --> 01:50:34.167
- Perhaps you know?
- What's wrong?

01:50:34.251 --> 01:50:36.667
Stop. Don't interrupt.

01:50:37.959 --> 01:50:39.959
If you know,

01:50:41.292 --> 01:50:44.334
but you can't tell me now,

01:50:44.917 --> 01:50:47.959
perhaps one day you will.

01:50:48.626 --> 01:50:50.459
What are you talking about?

01:50:50.626 --> 01:50:53.251
I don't understand a thing, honestly.

01:50:54.417 --> 01:50:56.626
You don't want to tell me.

01:50:58.126 --> 01:51:00.334
You're afraid.

01:51:01.084 --> 01:51:03.792
Then I'll tell you.

01:51:05.667 --> 01:51:07.417
I'm not Hari.

01:51:08.459 --> 01:51:10.792
Hari is dead.

01:51:11.334 --> 01:51:13.751
She poisoned herself.

01:51:14.876 --> 01:51:17.876
I'm somebody else.

01:51:17.959 --> 01:51:20.001
Who told you this?

01:51:20.626 --> 01:51:23.834
- Sartorius just told me.
- Last night.

01:51:27.751 --> 01:51:30.459
It would have been better
if you had told me yourself.

01:51:30.626 --> 01:51:33.584
My God, what's the difference?

01:51:38.959 --> 01:51:41.626
How have you lived all this time?

01:51:42.667 --> 01:51:44.667
Were you in love with anyone?

01:51:44.751 --> 01:51:46.417
I don't know.

01:51:46.501 --> 01:51:48.334
Did you ever think of me?

01:51:48.542 --> 01:51:51.667
Yes, but not all the time.

01:51:53.876 --> 01:51:56.376
Only when I felt unhappy.

01:52:02.542 --> 01:52:07.251
You know, it feels like
somebody is manipulating us.

01:52:09.042 --> 01:52:14.084
And the longer this fog lasts,
the worse it will be for you in the end.

01:52:14.417 --> 01:52:16.792
Particularly for you, Kris.

01:52:18.334 --> 01:52:20.376
How can I help you?

01:52:22.751 --> 01:52:24.251
Tell me.

01:52:24.376 --> 01:52:30.042
And her, the other one,
what happened to her?

01:52:38.959 --> 01:52:40.792
We argued.

01:52:41.667 --> 01:52:44.709
Towards the end, we argued a great deal.

01:52:44.917 --> 01:52:47.876
I gathered my things and left.

01:52:49.251 --> 01:52:52.709
She made me understand
without saying it directly,

01:52:53.376 --> 01:52:57.626
but when you live with someone for a
long time, such things aren't necessary.

01:52:59.292 --> 01:53:01.376
I was certain they were just words,

01:53:01.459 --> 01:53:04.542
but then I remembered that I'd left

01:53:06.542 --> 01:53:09.167
the laboratory specimens
in the refrigerator.

01:53:10.792 --> 01:53:14.959
I had brought them from the laboratory
and explained how they worked.

01:53:15.042 --> 01:53:16.792
I was afraid.

01:53:17.292 --> 01:53:19.626
I wanted to go to her.

01:53:19.751 --> 01:53:23.584
But then I thought it would look like
I had taken her words seriously.

01:53:24.084 --> 01:53:27.251
After three days, I couldn't take it
anymore and I went to see her.

01:53:27.417 --> 01:53:30.501
When I got there,
she was already dead.

01:53:30.959 --> 01:53:33.792
There was a needle mark on her arm.

01:53:36.167 --> 01:53:38.167
Like this?

01:53:46.792 --> 01:53:49.459
Why did she do it?

01:53:50.626 --> 01:53:54.876
She probably sensed
that I didn't really love her.

01:53:59.292 --> 01:54:01.167
But now I do.

01:54:13.001 --> 01:54:15.001
- Kris.
- What?

01:54:15.959 --> 01:54:17.792
I love you.

01:54:23.334 --> 01:54:25.584
Sleep.

01:54:25.667 --> 01:54:27.626
I don't know how to sleep.

01:54:29.417 --> 01:54:34.792
It's not sleep.
It's somehow around me.

01:54:37.251 --> 01:54:42.084
It's as if it weren't just inside of me,
but much farther away.

01:54:42.709 --> 01:54:46.876
It's probably still sleep.

01:55:27.334 --> 01:55:30.792
So, it looks like our guest of honour
isn't showing up.

01:55:34.834 --> 01:55:38.167
- Why?
- Perhaps he has guests.

01:56:34.167 --> 01:56:37.001
Everyone's already here?

01:56:40.292 --> 01:56:43.417
You're an hour and a half late.

01:56:49.959 --> 01:56:52.501
What's that you're reading?

01:56:58.167 --> 01:57:00.417
It's all rubbish.

01:57:02.626 --> 01:57:04.459
Rubbish.

01:57:06.292 --> 01:57:08.126
Where is it...

01:57:13.959 --> 01:57:15.667
Here.

01:57:18.959 --> 01:57:21.834
"They come at night.

01:57:23.542 --> 01:57:26.501
But one must sleep sometime."

01:57:27.626 --> 01:57:30.001
That's the problem.

01:57:31.334 --> 01:57:35.251
Mankind has lost the ability to sleep.

01:57:41.292 --> 01:57:46.334
You'd better read.
I'm a little excited.

01:57:48.626 --> 01:57:51.584
"I know only one thing, señor.
When I...

01:58:03.126 --> 01:58:07.459
When I sleep, I know no fear,
no hope, no trouble, no bliss.

01:58:07.542 --> 01:58:09.751
Blessings on him who invented sleep.

01:58:12.126 --> 01:58:15.709
The common coin
that purchases all things,

01:58:15.792 --> 01:58:17.834
the balance that levels
shepherd and king,

01:58:17.917 --> 01:58:20.126
fool and wise man.

01:58:20.209 --> 01:58:22.792
There is only one bad thing
about sound sleep.

01:58:22.876 --> 01:58:26.042
They say it closely resembles death."

01:58:26.126 --> 01:58:30.959
"Never before, Sancho, have I heard you
speak so elegantly as now."

01:58:33.876 --> 01:58:38.959
That's good, but perhaps
you'll let me say something now?

01:58:39.959 --> 01:58:42.751
I propose a toast to Snaut,

01:58:43.334 --> 01:58:48.126
to his bravery,
to his devotion to duty.

01:58:48.209 --> 01:58:51.001
To science and to Snaut.

01:58:51.292 --> 01:58:54.584
Science? Nonsense.

01:58:55.792 --> 01:59:01.667
In this situation, mediocrity and genius
are equally useless.

01:59:02.834 --> 01:59:08.126
We have no interest
in conquering any cosmos.

01:59:08.959 --> 01:59:13.126
We want to extend the Earth
to the borders of the cosmos.

01:59:13.792 --> 01:59:16.251
We don't know what to do
with other worlds.

01:59:16.334 --> 01:59:18.917
We don't need other worlds.

01:59:19.042 --> 01:59:22.126
We need a mirror.

01:59:22.459 --> 01:59:26.542
We struggle for contact,
but we'll never find it.

01:59:27.001 --> 01:59:29.542
We're in the foolish human
predicament

01:59:29.626 --> 01:59:33.459
of striving for a goal that he fears,

01:59:33.626 --> 01:59:35.751
that he has no need for.

01:59:36.584 --> 01:59:40.751
Man needs man.

01:59:48.376 --> 01:59:50.667
Let's drink to Gibarian.

01:59:50.834 --> 01:59:52.792
To his memory.

01:59:52.876 --> 01:59:56.042
Even though he was frightened.

02:00:08.626 --> 02:00:11.542
No, Gibarian was not frightened.

02:00:14.834 --> 02:00:17.542
There are worse things.

02:00:19.834 --> 02:00:23.042
He died of hopelessness.

02:00:24.959 --> 02:00:28.376
He thought all this
was happening only to him.

02:00:28.459 --> 02:00:30.501
My God.

02:00:31.292 --> 02:00:33.376
All these heartbreaking lamentations

02:00:33.459 --> 02:00:35.584
are nothing but
second-rate Dostoevsky.

02:00:36.417 --> 02:00:38.292
Who are you to judge?

02:00:38.376 --> 02:00:41.084
I know why I'm here.
I'm working.

02:00:41.792 --> 02:00:44.417
Man was created by nature
so he could learn her ways.

02:00:46.709 --> 02:00:50.417
In his endless search for the truth,
man is condemned to knowledge.

02:00:50.834 --> 02:00:53.209
Everything else is whim.

02:00:54.626 --> 02:00:57.042
Permit me to ask,
my esteemed colleague:

02:00:57.126 --> 02:00:59.709
Why have you come to Solaris?

02:01:00.709 --> 02:01:04.376
- What do you mean, why?
- Well, are you working a lot?

02:01:04.459 --> 02:01:07.584
Forgive me, but aside from
the romance with your ex-wife,

02:01:07.667 --> 02:01:09.917
nothing seems to interest you.

02:01:10.001 --> 02:01:13.209
You spend all day lounging in
a bed of noble thoughts,

02:01:13.292 --> 02:01:16.209
and that's how
you carry out your duty.

02:01:16.459 --> 02:01:19.292
You've lost touch with reality.

02:01:19.584 --> 02:01:21.792
Forgive me, but you're simply an idler.

02:01:21.876 --> 02:01:23.459
Enough.

02:01:23.542 --> 02:01:27.209
Let's try to be pleasant.
We'll drink to Gibarian.

02:01:27.292 --> 02:01:29.376
Not to Gibarian, but to Man.

02:01:29.459 --> 02:01:31.584
Are you saying
Gibarian was not a man?

02:01:31.667 --> 02:01:35.126
Stop it, Kris.
Let's not fight.

02:01:35.292 --> 02:01:40.126
After all, it's my birthday.
It's my day.

02:01:40.251 --> 02:01:41.959
Of course.

02:01:42.959 --> 02:01:46.292
I think that Kris Kelvin

02:01:47.459 --> 02:01:50.417
is more consistent than both of you.

02:01:50.542 --> 02:01:53.626
In inhuman conditions,
he has behaved humanely.

02:01:53.709 --> 02:01:57.251
And you act
as if none of this concerns you,

02:01:57.334 --> 02:02:02.209
and consider your guests -
it seems that's what you call us -

02:02:02.292 --> 02:02:05.417
something external, a hindrance.

02:02:05.751 --> 02:02:09.667
But it's a part of you.
It's your conscience.

02:02:13.501 --> 02:02:15.792
And Kris loves me.

02:02:19.126 --> 02:02:22.167
Perhaps it's not me he loves,

02:02:22.834 --> 02:02:26.501
but he's simply protecting himself.

02:02:27.584 --> 02:02:30.209
He wants me alive.

02:02:30.959 --> 02:02:33.417
That's not the point.
It doesn't matter why Man loves.

02:02:33.501 --> 02:02:35.584
It's different for everyone.

02:02:35.959 --> 02:02:38.626
It's not Kris.

02:02:39.126 --> 02:02:40.834
It's you.

02:02:40.917 --> 02:02:43.834
I hate you all.
- I would ask you...

02:02:43.917 --> 02:02:47.417
Please don't interrupt me.
I'm a woman, after all.

02:02:47.501 --> 02:02:49.542
You're not a woman
and you're not a human being.

02:02:49.626 --> 02:02:51.542
Understand that,

02:02:51.626 --> 02:02:54.542
if you're capable
of understanding anything.

02:02:57.001 --> 02:03:00.001
There is no Hari. She's dead.

02:03:03.209 --> 02:03:06.834
You're just a reproduction,

02:03:07.292 --> 02:03:09.709
a mechanical reproduction.

02:03:09.792 --> 02:03:12.876
A copy. A matrix.

02:03:21.667 --> 02:03:23.292
Yes.

02:03:25.626 --> 02:03:27.584
Perhaps.

02:03:36.459 --> 02:03:38.126
But I...

02:03:38.709 --> 02:03:42.251
I am becoming a human being.

02:03:45.876 --> 02:03:48.876
I can feel just as deeply as you.

02:03:50.209 --> 02:03:52.292
Believe me.

02:03:54.459 --> 02:03:57.334
I can already get by without him.

02:03:59.084 --> 02:04:00.501
I...

02:04:03.626 --> 02:04:05.542
love him.

02:04:07.792 --> 02:04:10.084
I am a human being.

02:04:10.792 --> 02:04:12.292
You...

02:04:13.626 --> 02:04:16.209
you're very cruel.

02:05:10.834 --> 02:05:13.417
Get up. Get up right now.

02:05:21.626 --> 02:05:23.709
My dear man.

02:05:29.126 --> 02:05:31.709
Nothing could be easier.

02:05:35.959 --> 02:05:38.626
We've wasted time arguing.

02:05:39.334 --> 02:05:43.959
We're losing our dignity
and human character.

02:05:46.501 --> 02:05:50.959
You're human, each in your own way.

02:05:52.084 --> 02:05:54.626
That's why you argue.

02:05:56.042 --> 02:05:58.459
I hope I'm not bothering you.

02:06:02.209 --> 02:06:04.709
You're a good man...

02:06:05.001 --> 02:06:08.376
but you look awful.

02:06:15.626 --> 02:06:18.084
I've really lost heart.

02:06:19.251 --> 02:06:22.292
Help me out, will you?

02:06:26.334 --> 02:06:31.542
Doesn't a man
who's ready to give up his life

02:06:31.626 --> 02:06:36.542
just to make cursed contact

02:06:36.626 --> 02:06:40.251
in order to know more about it
have the right to get drunk?

02:06:40.334 --> 02:06:43.792
He has every right.

02:06:45.376 --> 02:06:49.292
Do you believe in our mission, Kelvin?

02:06:50.667 --> 02:06:52.626
I'm not going to bed yet.

02:06:52.834 --> 02:06:55.251
It's important not to fall asleep.

02:06:56.001 --> 02:06:58.667
I'm going to see Faust.

02:06:59.834 --> 02:07:03.709
In the laboratory, our Faust -
Sartorius -

02:07:03.792 --> 02:07:06.792
is seeking a remedy for immortality.

02:07:06.876 --> 02:07:08.751
While we...

02:07:21.876 --> 02:07:27.417
Listen, let's open these hatches
and shout down below.

02:07:27.876 --> 02:07:30.417
It would suddenly hear.

02:07:30.834 --> 02:07:34.459
But what should we call it?

02:07:35.917 --> 02:07:41.042
We could show violence to it.

02:07:41.792 --> 02:07:44.376
Or, better yet, pray to it.

02:07:44.459 --> 02:07:45.917
What's wrong?

02:07:46.001 --> 02:07:48.709
I think I shut the door to the library.
She's there alone.

02:07:48.792 --> 02:07:51.167
Go. I feel better already.

02:07:51.251 --> 02:07:53.667
The station is changing its orbit.

02:07:54.167 --> 02:07:59.792
At 5am there will be
thirty seconds of weightlessness.

02:08:00.292 --> 02:08:02.709
Don't forget.

02:11:24.792 --> 02:11:27.626
Forgive me, my darling.
I was lost in thought.

02:11:29.792 --> 02:11:32.167
Is something wrong?

02:11:33.334 --> 02:11:36.459
No, nothing.

02:11:37.626 --> 02:11:39.792
Everything's fine.

02:15:32.001 --> 02:15:34.292
She drank liquid oxygen.

02:15:36.292 --> 02:15:38.959
She did it out of despair.

02:15:39.251 --> 02:15:41.376
It'll get worse.

02:15:41.459 --> 02:15:44.792
The more she's with you,
the more human she'll become.

02:15:45.334 --> 02:15:48.917
- Learn from Sartorius' example.
- Thanks for the advice.

02:15:53.542 --> 02:15:55.792
What do you intend to do?

02:15:55.959 --> 02:15:58.792
Wait until she returns.

02:15:58.959 --> 02:16:02.126
And then what?
Leave the station?

02:16:06.501 --> 02:16:11.917
Kris, she can only live here,
on the station. You know that.

02:16:13.459 --> 02:16:15.751
What can I do?

02:16:16.251 --> 02:16:17.959
I love her.
- Which one?

02:16:18.042 --> 02:16:23.167
Her, or the one in the rocket?
You can pull her in from space.

02:16:23.251 --> 02:16:25.834
She will appear again
and she'll keep appearing.

02:16:26.876 --> 02:16:30.626
Don't turn a scientific problem
into a common love story.

02:16:34.709 --> 02:16:37.584
I had a feeling this would end badly.

02:16:41.876 --> 02:16:43.792
You should help her.

02:17:00.584 --> 02:17:02.709
What a ghastly sight.

02:17:03.959 --> 02:17:09.626
I can never get used
to all these resurrections.

02:19:02.001 --> 02:19:04.126
Is it me?

02:19:10.626 --> 02:19:12.084
What?

02:19:18.251 --> 02:19:19.917
Why?

02:19:21.459 --> 02:19:23.126
Why?

02:19:26.084 --> 02:19:29.001
No, it's not me.

02:19:33.626 --> 02:19:36.042
It's... I'm... not Hari...

02:19:36.126 --> 02:19:41.001
And you... you...

02:19:41.334 --> 02:19:44.209
- Don't, Hari.
- I'm not Hari.

02:19:46.876 --> 02:19:49.167
Very well.

02:19:49.251 --> 02:19:51.917
Maybe your appearance
is supposed to be torture.

02:19:52.001 --> 02:19:53.751
Maybe it's a favour from the Ocean.

02:19:53.834 --> 02:19:58.751
What does it matter
when you're worth more to me

02:19:58.834 --> 02:20:01.209
than any science could ever be?

02:20:02.126 --> 02:20:03.876
Do I look a lot like her?

02:20:03.959 --> 02:20:07.126
No, you looked like her.

02:20:07.209 --> 02:20:10.584
But now you - and not her -
are the real Hari.

02:20:10.667 --> 02:20:13.417
Tell me...

02:20:14.084 --> 02:20:18.376
Do I disgust you? I'm so...

02:20:23.126 --> 02:20:26.084
I disgust you.
- No, Hari. That's not true.

02:20:26.167 --> 02:20:28.376
- You're lying.
- It's not true. Stop it.

02:20:28.459 --> 02:20:31.001
- I must be disgusting.
- Stop it.

02:20:38.084 --> 02:20:39.959
Don't touch me.

02:21:29.042 --> 02:21:31.334
I love you.

02:21:35.542 --> 02:21:37.584
What's the matter?

02:21:41.626 --> 02:21:44.917
Nothing.

02:21:50.834 --> 02:21:53.501
I'm not going back to Earth.

02:21:54.084 --> 02:21:58.292
I'll live here with you on the station.

02:21:59.084 --> 02:22:00.792
You know...

02:22:04.584 --> 02:22:06.959
I'm afraid.

02:24:15.042 --> 02:24:17.709
It looks like it's showing
some activity.

02:24:17.792 --> 02:24:20.459
Your encephalogram helped.

02:24:21.917 --> 02:24:23.626
You know...

02:24:23.792 --> 02:24:28.334
whenever we show pity,
we ravage ourselves.

02:24:28.626 --> 02:24:31.126
Perhaps it's true...

02:24:31.292 --> 02:24:36.167
Suffering makes life seem

02:24:36.334 --> 02:24:38.584
dismal and suspect.

02:24:42.626 --> 02:24:44.917
But I won't accept that.

02:24:48.709 --> 02:24:51.292
No, I won't accept that.

02:24:55.959 --> 02:25:01.792
Is that which is indispensable to life
also harmful to it?

02:25:02.959 --> 02:25:07.834
No, it's not harmful.
Of course it's not harmful.

02:25:09.001 --> 02:25:11.209
Remember Tolstoy?

02:25:11.917 --> 02:25:16.667
His suffering over the impossibility
of loving mankind as a whole?

02:25:19.376 --> 02:25:22.709
How much time has passed since then?

02:25:23.292 --> 02:25:27.292
Somehow I can't figure it out.
Help me.

02:25:30.084 --> 02:25:32.084
See, I love you.

02:25:32.167 --> 02:25:36.292
But love is a feeling
we can experience

02:25:36.376 --> 02:25:39.001
but never explain.

02:25:39.292 --> 02:25:41.459
One can explain the concept.

02:25:41.542 --> 02:25:44.584
You love that which you can lose:

02:25:44.667 --> 02:25:48.001
Yourself, a woman, a homeland.

02:25:48.959 --> 02:25:54.167
Until today, love was simply
unattainable to mankind, to the Earth.

02:25:54.251 --> 02:25:56.251
Do you understand me, Snaut?

02:25:56.334 --> 02:26:00.792
There are so few of us.
A few billion altogether. A handful.

02:26:02.251 --> 02:26:06.792
We could be here in order
to experience people

02:26:07.292 --> 02:26:08.959
as a reason for love.

02:26:14.626 --> 02:26:16.917
He seems to have a fever.

02:26:18.251 --> 02:26:22.876
How did Gibarian die?
You still haven't told me.

02:26:23.417 --> 02:26:26.084
I'll tell you. Later.

02:26:26.792 --> 02:26:30.876
Gibarian didn't die of fear.
He died of shame.

02:26:30.959 --> 02:26:36.126
Shame - the feeling
that will save mankind.

02:29:04.042 --> 02:29:06.042
Mama, I...

02:29:09.292 --> 02:29:11.709
I'm two hours late.

02:29:11.792 --> 02:29:13.501
I know.

02:29:14.626 --> 02:29:16.459
How was your trip?

02:29:17.417 --> 02:29:22.292
Fine. I'm a little tired,
but it was fine.

02:29:37.792 --> 02:29:42.542
My God, it's running slow again.

02:29:43.417 --> 02:29:45.084
I'll go adjust it.

02:29:45.167 --> 02:29:47.251
You've got plenty of time.

02:30:14.959 --> 02:30:19.292
You know, it's really embarrassing,
but for some reason...

02:30:22.792 --> 02:30:25.917
I've completely forgotten your face.

02:30:26.751 --> 02:30:29.084
You don't look well.

02:30:31.167 --> 02:30:32.334
Are you happy?

02:30:32.417 --> 02:30:36.126
Somehow that concept
seems irrelevant here.

02:30:37.501 --> 02:30:41.292
That's really a pity.

02:30:45.084 --> 02:30:47.959
I'm very lonesome now.

02:31:00.084 --> 02:31:03.126
Why do you hurt our feelings?

02:31:03.209 --> 02:31:05.001
What have you been waiting for?

02:31:06.126 --> 02:31:08.834
Why haven't you called?

02:31:26.834 --> 02:31:29.792
You're leading
some sort of strange life.

02:31:30.501 --> 02:31:33.834
You're filthy and unkempt.

02:31:35.542 --> 02:31:38.126
How did you make
such a mess of yourself?

02:31:43.209 --> 02:31:45.209
What's this?

02:31:46.959 --> 02:31:49.459
Wait here. I'll be right back.

02:33:46.542 --> 02:33:49.667
How are you?
Everything all right?

02:33:49.751 --> 02:33:51.834
Where's Hari?

02:34:03.126 --> 02:34:04.959
What's that?

02:34:05.209 --> 02:34:07.584
There's no more Hari.

02:34:31.667 --> 02:34:36.876
"Kris, it's terrible that I had
to deceive you,

02:34:36.959 --> 02:34:39.501
but there was no other way.

02:34:40.959 --> 02:34:43.834
This is best for both of us.

02:34:49.542 --> 02:34:52.501
I asked them myself.

02:34:53.501 --> 02:34:57.251
You mustn't blame anyone.

02:34:59.042 --> 02:35:00.917
Hari."

02:35:05.209 --> 02:35:07.584
She did it for you.

02:35:18.042 --> 02:35:20.959
Snaut, listen.

02:35:22.209 --> 02:35:24.626
Later, Kris. Calm down.

02:35:25.292 --> 02:35:28.917
How... how did it...

02:35:30.292 --> 02:35:33.917
The annihilator?
A burst of light and wind.

02:35:43.459 --> 02:35:45.376
Yes.

02:35:46.084 --> 02:35:49.792
Things weren't working out
between us towards the end.

02:35:54.417 --> 02:35:56.584
Listen, Snaut.

02:35:57.292 --> 02:36:00.667
Why are we being tortured like this?

02:36:02.667 --> 02:36:07.376
In my opinion, we have lost
our sense of the cosmic.

02:36:07.792 --> 02:36:09.959
The ancients understood it perfectly.

02:36:10.042 --> 02:36:13.792
They never would have asked
why or what for.

02:36:14.209 --> 02:36:16.959
Remember the myth of Sisyphus.

02:36:18.542 --> 02:36:21.876
Since we transmitted
your encephalogram,

02:36:21.959 --> 02:36:25.459
none of the guests have come back.

02:36:25.626 --> 02:36:29.667
Something incomprehensible is starting
to take place in the Ocean.

02:36:29.792 --> 02:36:32.417
Islands have begun to form
on the surface.

02:36:32.501 --> 02:36:36.417
First one. Then the next day
there were several more.

02:36:36.501 --> 02:36:39.792
Are you trying to tell me
that it understood us?

02:36:40.959 --> 02:36:42.834
That quickly?

02:36:43.251 --> 02:36:47.626
But at least there's hope, Kris?

02:36:55.209 --> 02:36:58.792
- How old are you?
- Fifty-two. Why?

02:36:59.876 --> 02:37:01.959
Have you been here long?

02:37:03.126 --> 02:37:06.501
- You must have seen my forms.
- I did.

02:37:07.709 --> 02:37:13.126
Listen, having spent so many years
here on the station,

02:37:14.334 --> 02:37:19.042
do you still feel a clear connection
to your life down there?

02:37:19.334 --> 02:37:22.167
You like dire questions.

02:37:22.334 --> 02:37:25.709
Soon you'll ask me
about the meaning of life.

02:37:25.792 --> 02:37:28.292
Wait. Don't be ironic.

02:37:28.459 --> 02:37:30.751
It's a banal question.

02:37:31.876 --> 02:37:34.251
When man is happy,

02:37:34.459 --> 02:37:39.626
the meaning of life and other
eternal themes rarely interest him.

02:37:41.001 --> 02:37:45.042
These questions should be asked
at the end of one's life.

02:37:49.292 --> 02:37:53.292
But we don't know when life will end.

02:37:53.376 --> 02:37:55.376
That's why we're in such a hurry.

02:37:55.459 --> 02:37:57.334
Don't rush.

02:37:57.417 --> 02:38:03.417
The happiest people are those who are
not interested in these cursed questions.

02:38:03.501 --> 02:38:06.376
To ask is always
the desire to know.

02:38:06.459 --> 02:38:10.709
Yet the preservation of
simple human truths requires mystery.

02:38:10.959 --> 02:38:14.959
The mysteries of happiness,
death and love.

02:38:15.084 --> 02:38:19.459
You could be right,
but try not to think about all that now.

02:38:20.292 --> 02:38:25.334
To think about it
is to know the day of one's death.

02:38:27.126 --> 02:38:31.459
Not knowing that day
makes us practically immortal.

02:38:36.959 --> 02:38:38.792
Fine, then.

02:38:39.126 --> 02:38:41.917
In any event,
my mission is finished.

02:38:42.084 --> 02:38:45.959
But what next?
Return to Earth?

02:38:46.709 --> 02:38:48.959
Little by little,
everything will return to normal.

02:38:49.042 --> 02:38:51.876
I'll even find
new interests and acquaintances.

02:38:53.001 --> 02:38:55.959
But I won't be able
to give myself to them fully.

02:38:56.667 --> 02:38:58.542
Never.

02:39:00.917 --> 02:39:03.376
Do I have the right to turn down

02:39:03.459 --> 02:39:08.542
even an imagined possibility
of contact with this Ocean

02:39:09.042 --> 02:39:14.001
which my race has been trying
to understand for decades?

02:39:14.751 --> 02:39:16.709
Should I remain here?

02:39:16.959 --> 02:39:21.292
Among things and objects
we both touched?

02:39:21.751 --> 02:39:24.334
Which still bear the memory
of our breath?

02:39:24.501 --> 02:39:26.584
What for?

02:39:26.667 --> 02:39:29.292
In the hope that she'll return?

02:39:29.626 --> 02:39:32.626
But I don't harbour this hope.

02:39:33.959 --> 02:39:36.001
The only thing left for me

02:39:36.167 --> 02:39:38.876
is to wait.

02:39:40.001 --> 02:39:43.917
I don't know what for.
New miracles?

02:39:50.084 --> 02:39:51.834
Are you tired?

02:39:52.292 --> 02:39:55.626
No, I feel great.

02:39:55.709 --> 02:39:57.459
You know, Kris...

02:39:57.584 --> 02:40:00.626
I think it's time
you returned to Earth.

02:40:02.292 --> 02:40:04.417
You think so?
